From 0f1c3169a52dd67613da22ed85e13429abe22f37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 19:29:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 02: reusable workflows (named, parameterised step
 sequences)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds workflows.py — a project-scoped workflow layer backed by two new
SQLite tables (workflows, workflow_runs) that live in the same DB as
memory entries. A workflow is a named, ordered list of WorkflowStep
prompt templates with {placeholder} variables filled at run time via
str.format_map(). Executing a workflow calls run_task() once per step
in order; stop_on_failure halts and marks remaining steps 'skipped' if
any step returns a non-'complete' status.

New modules / files:
  workflows.py         — WorkflowStep, Workflow, WorkflowResult,
                         StepResult dataclasses; save_workflow (upsert
                         on project_id+name), get_workflow, list_workflows,
                         delete_workflow, run_workflow, list_workflow_runs;
                         _start/_finish_workflow_run internal helpers;
                         WORKFLOW_SCHEMA applied on top of memory's existing
                         schema so the projects FK constraint is always met.
  test_workflows.py    — 24 tests across 4 classes:
                         TestWorkflowCRUD (9), TestWorkflowStep (4),
                         TestRunWorkflow (8), TestWorkflowToolsInForge (3).

Changes to forge.py:
  - `import workflows as _workflows` added.
  - Four new tool functions: save_workflow_tool, run_workflow_tool,
    list_workflows_tool, recall_workflow_runs_tool.
  - Four new ToolSpec entries in TOOLS dict (risks: write / execute /
    read / read).
  - System prompt extended with full docs + JSON examples for all four
    workflow tools.

Design notes:
  - Workflows are data, not code — stored as JSON step lists, never
    executable code, so there is nothing to sandbox.
  - run_workflow_tool passes forge.run_task as the executor, keeping
    the evidence-ledger / completion-checking loop for every step.
  - DB_PATH in workflows.py re-exports memory.DB_PATH so both modules
    patch correctly in tests with patch.object(workflows, "DB_PATH", …)
    alongside patch.object(memory, "DB_PATH", …).
  - Deferred `import forge` inside run_workflow() avoids a circular
    import at module load time (forge imports workflows; workflows must
    not import forge at the top level).

All 96 tests pass (72 prior + 24 new); no stray .db files produced.

